Subject: [PATCH 3349/3799] soh: rename func_800FF334 -> Arena_Unused

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: declared taking an Arena with no definition and no caller in the tree
Defined in soh/include/functions.h.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/include/functions.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/include/functions.h b/soh/include/functions.h
index dd4cae794..aa1b29fe7 100644
--- a/soh/include/functions.h
+++ b/soh/include/functions.h
@@ -2297,7 +2297,8 @@ void ArenaImpl_GetSizes(Arena* arena, u32* outMaxFree, u32* outFree, u32* outAll
 void __osDisplayArena(Arena* arena);
 void ArenaImpl_FaultClient(Arena* arena);
 s32 __osCheckArena(Arena* arena);
-u8 func_800FF334(Arena* arena);
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_800FF334: declared taking an Arena with no definition and no caller in the tree
+u8 Arena_Unused(Arena* arena);  // was func_800FF334 [LLM:GUESS]
 s32 PrintUtils_VPrintf(PrintCallback* pfn, const char* fmt, va_list args);
 s32 PrintUtils_Printf(PrintCallback* pfn, const char* fmt, ...);
 void Sleep_Cycles(OSTime cycles);
